  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. It replaces a record naming the owner as reviewer, because that record's fingerprint no longer matched. Read sdk_binding_core.adapter and the eleven sdk_typescript units whose inputs moved. The TypeScript transport was split from one transport.ts into transport.ts plus transport_{binding,config,continuation,envelope,errors,freshness,verify}.ts. I compared the old and new code in order. The constructor's validation is one validateConfig that runs the same five checks in the same order with the same conditions and messages (concurrency bound, continuation rounds, clock skew within the bound, a complete trust anchor, a non-empty-string denylist array). send() still refuses a client-side response, runs a notification under the semaphore with only that send failing, and for a request maps ConnectionClosed to a rethrow and McpReError, McpReSdkError and any other Error to the same correlated error codes (plainErrorWireCode is the old core-code-or-mcp-re-sdk-prefix rule); the slot is taken, the closed state is refused after acquiring it and the abort race still wraps the work, so a request queued at the semaphore when close() lands is neither signed nor posted. A leg still checks the abort signal first, draws created, expires, the bindings and then the checked nonce in that order (the signing basis evaluates bindings before the nonce), signs, records the correlation, posts, verifies with the clock read for the call, and retires its entry on a rejection or terminal reply; the rejection error carries the same code and the same requestBound and execution facts; the pause records the input-required handles without consuming, calls the hook, increments the round, refuses past the ceiling and with no handler (answerHandlerFor) before the abort check and the handler, refuses a declined or non-object answer after it (collectAnswer), and builds the next leg from the same params plus inputResponses and requestState under the derived id; the finally still abandons every outstanding entry. verifyReply and verifyAcknowledgement pass the core the same arguments in the same order, and the reply rebuild (plainMcpReply, verifiedResult) checks a non-object, a method, both and neither members as before. The nonce floor and default clock are unchanged. The unit tests are unchanged apart from two comment and skip-reporting edits in files no unit cites; the binding core takes McpMessage through build_signed_message with the same request-or-notification dispatch. The claim, scope and premises are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane and the SDK matrix lane were not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
